From 620fc3191f5829bc467ef9e041a43ba6d85d9624 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dnz3d4c <dnz3d4c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:45:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Accept the Korean confirm-button label
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PressFocusedOk matched the confirm button by label against
["Ok", "Bestaetigen"], both German. On the Korean client the button reads
"확인", so nothing matched and character creation could not be left at all:
the log shows "PressOk: kein Ok-Button in '_CharaMakeFeature'" once per
Enter press.

The label is measured, not guessed. A live node dump of KR
2026.08.05.0000.0000 shows the confirm button as Comp(1001) with a text
child "확인" in both _CharaMakeProgress and _CharaMakeFeature, and the
button component itself carries the visible flag (F=0x2033) even though
its text child does not - which is what TryClickButton tests.

Confirmed in game: character creation completes end to end after this.

This is a Korean hardcode in a list that is already a German hardcode. The
right shape is a per-locale label set, the same generalisation the other
five game-text matches need. Left for that change rather than done twice.

Build: 0 warnings 0 errors against 7.51.0.8667 and against 7.55.1.8875
In-game: confirmed, character creation finished

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FF14Accessibility/Services/UIReaderService.cs | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FF14Accessibility/Services/UIReaderService.cs b/FF14Accessibility/Services/UIReaderService.cs
index c9e34fa..df9fa8c 100644
--- a/FF14Accessibility/Services/UIReaderService.cs
+++ b/FF14Accessibility/Services/UIReaderService.cs
@@ -7163,7 +7163,12 @@ public sealed class UIReaderService : IDisposable
     /// CharaMake*/TitleDCWorldMap so Enter keeps its game meaning elsewhere.
     /// </summary>
     // Confirm-button labels in priority order (German client).
-    private static readonly string[] ConfirmButtonLabels = ["Ok", "Bestätigen"];
+    // "확인" is the Korean client's label, read out of a live node dump of
+    // _CharaMakeProgress and _CharaMakeFeature (KR 2026.08.05.0000.0000,
+    // 2026-08-17): both confirm buttons are Comp(1001) with the text child
+    // "확인". Without it PressFocusedOk logs "kein Ok-Button" on every step of
+    // character creation and the appearance step cannot be left at all.
+    private static readonly string[] ConfirmButtonLabels = ["Ok", "Bestätigen", "확인"];
 
     public unsafe void PressFocusedOk()
     {
-- 
